/-!
# Lawvere–Stone Representation for Closure-Generated Proof Semirings

This file proves the main representation theorem: a closure-generated proof semiring
embeds into (and under spectral completeness, is isomorphic to) the semiring of
basis global sections of its structure sheaf on the prime congruence spectrum.

## Main definitions

* `ClosureGeneratedProofSemiring`: A commutative semiring with a closure operator.
* `StalkProduct P`: The product `∏_p P/p` over all prime congruences.
* `IsLocallyRepresentable`: The sheaf condition for sections.
* `basisGlobalSectionsSubsemiring`: Subsemiring of locally representable sections.
* `BasisGlobalSections P`: Type alias for the subsemiring.
* `toStalkProduct`: The evaluation map `P →+* StalkProduct P`.
* `toBasisGlobalSections`: The map into locally representable sections.

## Main results

* `toStalkProduct_eq_iff`: Pointwise characterization of equality.
* `toStalkProduct_injective`: Injectivity from prime separation.
* `toBasisGlobalSections_injective`: Injectivity for the subsemiring map.
* `toBasisGlobalSections_surjective`: Surjectivity under spectral completeness.
* `toBasisGlobalSections_bijective`: The full representation theorem.
* `toBasisGlobalSectionsEquiv`: Ring isomorphism `P ≃+* BasisGlobalSections P`.

## Mathematical significance

**Proof semantics is a sheaf-theoretic geometry over the prime congruence spectrum.**
Two proof values are equal iff all prime truth valuations identify them (injectivity),
and under spectral completeness, every compatible family of local truth values arises
from a unique global proof value (surjectivity).
-/

universe u

/-! ## The prime congruence spectrum

The spectrum below was used throughout this file but was never defined in the
project, so the file did not elaborate.  A **prime congruence** on a commutative
semiring is a ring congruence that is proper and satisfies the twisted-product
condition (Joó–Mincheva): it is the congruence-theoretic analogue of a prime ideal,
and for a ring it specialises to the congruence generated by a prime ideal.  The
spectrum carries the hull–kernel topology generated by the separating sets
`D(a,b) = {p | ¬ p.con a b}`. -/

/-- A prime congruence on a commutative semiring `P`. -/
structure PrimeConSpec (P : Type u) [CommSemiring P] where
  /-- The underlying ring congruence. -/
  con : RingCon P
  /-- The congruence is proper: it does not collapse `0` and `1`. -/
  proper : ¬ con 0 1
  /-- Twisted-product primality. -/
  prime : ∀ a b c d : P, con (a * c) (b * d) → con (a * d) (b * c) → con a b ∨ con c d

namespace PrimeConSpec

/-- The basic open set `D(a,b)` of primes that separate `a` from `b`. -/
def basicOpen {P : Type u} [CommSemiring P] (a b : P) : Set (PrimeConSpec P) :=
  {p | ¬ p.con a b}

/-- The hull–kernel (Zariski) topology on the prime congruence spectrum. -/
instance instTopologicalSpace {P : Type u} [CommSemiring P] :
    TopologicalSpace (PrimeConSpec P) :=
  TopologicalSpace.generateFrom {U | ∃ a b : P, U = basicOpen a b}


end PrimeConSpec

open PrimeConSpec

/-! ## Closure-Generated Proof Semiring -/

/-- A **closure-generated proof semiring** is a commutative semiring equipped with a
closure operator satisfying the Kuratowski axioms. -/
class ClosureGeneratedProofSemiring (P : Type u) extends CommSemiring P where
  closure : Set P → Set P
  closure_extensive : ∀ S : Set P, S ⊆ closure S
  closure_mono : ∀ {S T : Set P}, S ⊆ T → closure S ⊆ closure T
  closure_idem : ∀ S : Set P, closure (closure S) = closure S

variable {P : Type u} [CommSemiring P]

/-! ## The Stalk Product -/

/-- The **stalk product** `∏_p P/p` over all prime congruences. -/
def StalkProduct (P : Type u) [CommSemiring P] : Type u :=
  (p : PrimeConSpec P) → p.con.Quotient

noncomputable instance : CommSemiring (StalkProduct P) := Pi.commSemiring

/-- The canonical **evaluation map** `a ↦ ([a]_p)_p`. -/
noncomputable def toStalkProduct (P : Type u) [CommSemiring P] :
    P →+* StalkProduct P :=
  Pi.ringHom (fun p => p.con.mk')


